  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing CRM Views**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the CRM views. I\'ve begun listing the required templates, drawing from the provided screenshots. So far, I\'ve identified the \"Sidebar Navigation\" template as a key component, specifically noting the logo (a roofing icon) and brand details (\"Apex Roofing\" or \"Enterprise Management\"). I\'m also capturing the JSON spec color scheme for the sidebar.\n\n\n**Refining Sidebar Design**\n\nI\'m now refining the sidebar design. I\'m focusing on the \"Apex Roofing\" header with a roofing icon, just as in the images, plus the list of links (Dashboard, Leads, Claims, Production, Financials, Team). Icons are being carefully selected for each link. Settings and Support are placed at the bottom. A new project CTA with a stylish green button is also in design. Finally, I\'m setting up a unified state system within `src/types.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining State and Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into defining the app\'s state and components, and I\'m creating `src/types.ts` to share types app-wide. I\'m focusing on the \"Leads/Customers\" section, planning a dynamic list and a \"Leads Directory\" view. I\'m thinking of a timeline view with update inputs and a \"Lead File / Client File\" timeline with various tabs, including \"Seguros/Claims\" with insurance information and adjuster details.\n\n\n**Detailing Claim View**\n\nI\'m now detailing the claim view for #SF-99482-TX. The \"Documentos\" tab will show attached files. \"Producci\303\263n\" will link to the schedule. I\'m designing a pending tasks checklist widget for the right sidebar. I\'m also planning the AI Copilot panel with a client file summary, risk analysis, proactive alerts, and action suggestions, all integrated within the claim view.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Tables**\n\nI\'m now focused on the interactive items table for estimate #EST-2409-A for James Robertson. I\'m building editable fields for quantity and unit price, with dynamic updates for subtotal, taxes, total, and profit. I\'m including options to add and delete rows, and integrating a financial summary card. The current items listed are Architectural Shingles, Synthetic Underlayment, Ridge Venting, and Mano de Obra, with a warning tag on ridge venting.\n\n\n**Integrating AI Suggestions**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-powered suggestions within the interactive items table for James Robertson\'s estimate.  The AI Copilot now has alerts!  I\'m focusing on the \"Margen Inferior al Est\303\241ndar\" alert, which dynamically calculates the required labor price to reach a 30% margin, with an \"Auto-ajustar al 30%\" button. I\'m also including a \"Falta Reporte ITEL\" alert with an \"Adjuntar Reporte\" button. I also started building out the Main Dashboard. I\'ve designed KPI cards for Leads, Claims, Production, and Pending Payments. I\'m also building Critical Alerts for missing documentation.\n\n\n**Visualizing Workflow**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the workflow using Kanban boards. I\'ve designed columns for \"Scheduled,\" \"Material Ordered,\" \"In Progress,\" and \"QA Inspection.\" I\'m populating these columns with project cards, including project details and estimated completion times. For the \"Scheduled\" column, I have Anderson Residence. \"Material Ordered\" includes Chen Commercial, and \"In Progress\" shows the Martinez Estate and First Baptist Church projects.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the file `/src/types.ts` to define the TypeScript types, interfaces, and shared state for our roofing CRM, including Leads, Estimates, Kanban Columns, Invoices, Team members, and Copilot Chat history."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
