  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Backend Infrastructure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on establishing the Express backend infrastructure. I\'m reviewing the guidelines, including hosting on `0.0.0.0` at port 3000. It\'s crucial to set up the API routes prior to incorporating Vite middleware. I\'ll need to remember that production static file serving comes from `dist/` and falls back to `index`.\n\n\n**Developing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now creating the `/api/copilot` endpoint. It needs to handle `message`, `history`, and `context` input, then call the Gemini API using `@google/genai`. I\'m using `gemini-3.5-flash` and will structure the response with a `text` field. I need to make sure the headers are set properly, and will follow the `SKILL.md` example. I\'m checking the workspace for an existing `server.ts` file; it looks like I need to create it.\n\n\n**Implementing API Key Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on robust API key management. My goal is to prevent server crashes if the Gemini API key is missing. I\'m implementing lazy initialization to avoid immediate failures, and will also provide a user-friendly error message, guiding the user to configure the API key through the AI Studio settings. This proactive approach ensures a smoother developer experience.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the file `server.ts` to implement our full-stack Express backend. This server will handle API requests for the AI Copilot on the endpoint `/api/copilot` and integrate the Vite middleware for development (with static serving in production) on port `3000` and host `0.0.0.0`. It uses lazy initialization for the Gemini client to avoid crashes if the key is not set."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 212390780
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
