  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Deciding Component Structure**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed by writing the complete `/src/App.tsx` file. I\'m leaning toward including the recalculate helper function directly within the main component to keep state management focused and streamlined. It feels cleaner this way!\n\n\n**Defining Recalculation Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `recalculateEstimate` function. I\'ve fleshed out its basic structure. It iterates through items, calculating totals and categorizing costs for materials, labor, and fees. I\'m including the tax calculation and the total calculation. I\'m starting to think about profit margin cost.\n\n\n**Adjusting Profit Margin Target**\n\nI\'m now integrating profit margin control. Currently, the `recalculateEstimate` function calculates the profit margin based on costs. Now, I need to ensure it *targets* a 30% margin. This involves adjusting the cost calculations somehow to achieve the desired profit percentage. I will need to factor that into the logic.\n\n\n**Calculating Labor Unit Price**\n\nI\'m now determining how to find the target labor unit price. I\'ve broken it down step by step: Identify the labor item and quantity. Then, calculate the gross revenue needed for a 30% margin. Assuming the crew cost is a fixed $60/SQ. I\'ve determined how to calculate the cost of non-labor items and labor. Now, I need to calculate the Gross Selling Price needed to achieve a 30% profit margin.\n\n\n**Deriving Targeted Labor Price**\n\nI\'ve just distilled the logic for calculating the target labor unit price to hit a precise 30% profit margin, no matter the inputs. The core formula: I\'m determining the target Gross Selling Price, which is `Total Cost / (1 - 0.3)`. Then I derive the labor selling price needed by subtracting material and fee costs. Finally, I divide the labor selling price by the labor quantity, yielding the Labor Unit Price! This adapts perfectly to any customized table data. This is working great.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the main container file `/src/App.tsx`. This component handles the application\'s global reactive state (Leads, Claims Estimator, Production, Financials, Team Directory), calculates real-time estimate subtotals, margins, and taxes, orchestrates transitions between dashboards, and coordinates real-time AI Copilot chat submissions to our full-stack Express API."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 375378821
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
